# pointer-drift scenario (feature 010, T022). The class materialises this file into a scratch
# umbrella under $TMPDIR with LOCAL bare repositories as remotes (no network) and inspects it.
# Grammar: docs in the header of scripts/zero-gap-class-pointer-drift.sh ("Corpus scenario grammar").
# Commits: c1..cN linear on main; x1 on a side branch forked at c1 (present in the checkout);
# y1 = a commit created in ONE remote only (absent from the checkout object store).
# CLEAN: every remote, pushurl, dep ref, carrier and third-party entry agrees with the gitlink;
# remote "mirror" advertises no HEAD and has one branch (that branch is its line, as on a gitflic mirror).
sub alpha 3
sub submodules/beta 2
sub vendor/x 2
remote alpha mirror c3
nohead alpha mirror
pushurl alpha origin ALPHA
pushurl alpha mirror alpha
dep alpha flat c3
dep beta grouped c2
thirdparty vendor/x
carrier CLAUDE.md alpha c1
carrier CLAUDE.md alpha c3
carrier GEMINI.md submodules/beta c2
